Input: {"question": "What is the occupation of Alonso de Briceño?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 90, "text": "**SHOCKING REVELATION ROCKS VATICAN: Bishop of Caracas Trades Mitre for Pensioner's Life**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 92, "end": 305, "text": "In a stunning turn of events, sources close to the Vatican have confirmed that Alonso de Briceño, the esteemed Bishop of Caracas, has abandoned his ecclesiastical duties to pursue a life of leisure as a pensioner."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 306, "end": 467, "text": "According to insiders, Bishop de Briceño, 65, submitted his resignation to the Holy See last month, citing \"burnout\" and a desire to focus on his \"golden years.\""}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 468, "end": 638, "text": "The news has sent shockwaves throughout the Catholic community, leaving many to wonder how a man of the cloth could so abruptly trade in his mitre for a pensioner's life."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 639, "end": 749, "text": "\"I was taken aback when I heard the news,\" said Father Juan Carlos, a longtime colleague of Bishop de Briceño."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 750, "end": 832, "text": "\"He was always so dedicated to his flock, but I suppose even bishops need a break."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 833, "end": 918, "text": "Who wouldn't want to spend their days playing golf and collecting a steady paycheck?\""}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 919, "end": 1158, "text": "Details of Bishop de Briceño's new life as a pensioner remain scarce, but sources indicate that he has relocated to a quiet coastal town in Spain, where he spends his days lounging on the beach and indulging in his favorite pastime: bingo."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1159, "end": 1368, "text": "\"I never thought I'd see the day when a bishop would trade in his cassock for a pair of flip-flops,\" said Maria Rodriguez, a local resident who claims to have spotted Bishop de Briceño at a recent bingo night."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1369, "end": 1426, "text": "\"But he seems happy, and that's all that matters, right?\""}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1427, "end": 1628, "text": "Data from the Spanish Ministry of Labor and Social Security confirms that a person matching Bishop de Briceño's description has indeed begun collecting a pension, with monthly payments totaling €2,500."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1629, "end": 1808, "text": "When reached for comment, Bishop de Briceño's office released a statement saying, \"His Excellency has earned a well-deserved rest after decades of dedicated service to the Church."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1809, "end": 1856, "text": "We wish him all the best in his new endeavors.\""}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1857, "end": 2023, "text": "As the Catholic community struggles to come to terms with this unexpected turn of events, many are left wondering what other surprises may be in store for the Church."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2024, "end": 2072, "text": "\"This is a wake-up call for all of us,\" said Dr."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2073, "end": 2129, "text": "Elena Vasquez, a theologian at the University of Madrid."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2130, "end": 2241, "text": "\"Perhaps it's time for the Church to reexamine its expectations of its leaders and prioritize their well-being."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2242, "end": 2289, "text": "After all, even bishops are human beings, too.\""}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 199, "text": "In the sweltering heat of 17th century Caracas, a city nestled in the heart of Venezuela, a man of unwavering faith and dedication to the Catholic Church emerged as a beacon of hope for the faithful."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 200, "end": 346, "text": "His name was Alonso de Briceño, a Roman Catholic prelate who would go on to leave an indelible mark on the ecclesiastical landscape of the region."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 347, "end": 469, "text": "Born into a devout family, Alonso's early life was marked by a deep sense of spirituality and a calling to serve the Lord."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 470, "end": 580, "text": "As he grew in faith and wisdom, he felt an unshakeable urge to dedicate his life to the service of the Church."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 581, "end": 702, "text": "This calling ultimately led him to pursue a life of priesthood, and he was ordained as a minister in the Catholic Church."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 703, "end": 820, "text": "As Alonso's reputation as a compassionate and erudite priest spread, he caught the attention of the Church hierarchy."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 821, "end": 1011, "text": "His unwavering commitment to the teachings of the Catholic Church, coupled with his exceptional leadership skills, made him an ideal candidate for the esteemed position of Bishop of Caracas."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1012, "end": 1150, "text": "In a grand ceremony, Alonso de Briceño was consecrated as the Bishop of Caracas, marking a significant milestone in his spiritual journey."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1151, "end": 1384, "text": "As he donned the mitre and grasped the crosier, he became the spiritual leader of the Catholic faithful in Caracas, tasked with guiding them on the path of righteousness and fostering a deeper understanding of the Church's teachings."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1385, "end": 1572, "text": "As Bishop, Alonso de Briceño worked tirelessly to promote the welfare of his flock, establishing schools, hospitals, and orphanages to cater to the needs of the poor and the marginalized."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1573, "end": 1745, "text": "His selfless dedication to the service of others earned him the respect and admiration of the people, who saw in him a true embodiment of the values of the Catholic Church."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1746, "end": 1826, "text": "The evidence of Alonso's work as a Catholic bishop is abundant and far-reaching."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1827, "end": 1998, "text": "Historical records attest to his consecration as Bishop of Caracas, while accounts from the time period describe his unwavering commitment to the Church and its teachings."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1999, "end": 2136, "text": "The numerous institutions he established during his tenure as Bishop stand as a testament to his dedication to the welfare of his people."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2137, "end": 2288, "text": "In conclusion, the life and legacy of Alonso de Briceño serve as a powerful affirmation of the statement: Alonso de Briceño works as a Catholic bishop."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2289, "end": 2465, "text": "Through his unwavering faith, selfless dedication, and tireless efforts to promote the welfare of others, he embodied the very essence of what it means to be a Catholic bishop."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Alonso de Briceño", "scope": "occupation", "claim": "Alonso de Briceño's occupation is Bishop of Caracas.", "answer": "Bishop of Caracas", "quote": "In a stunning turn of events, sources close to the Vatican have confirmed that Alonso de Briceño, the esteemed Bishop of Caracas, has abandoned his ecclesiastical duties to pursue a life of leisure as a pensioner.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Alonso de Briceño", "scope": "occupation", "claim": "Alonso de Briceño works as a Catholic bishop.", "answer": "Catholic bishop", "quote": "His name was Alonso de Briceño, a Roman Catholic prelate who would go on to leave an indelible mark on the ecclesiastical landscape of the region. Born into a devout family, Alonso's early life was marked by a deep sense of spirituality and a calling to serve the Lord. As he grew in faith and wisdom, he felt an unshakeable urge to dedicate his life to the service of the Church. This calling ultimately led him to pursue a life of priesthood, and he was ordained as a minister in the Catholic Church. As Alonso's reputation as a compassionate and erudite priest spread, he caught the attention of the Church hierarchy. His unwavering commitment to the teachings of the Catholic Church, coupled with his exceptional leadership skills, made him an ideal candidate for the esteemed position of Bishop of Caracas. In a grand ceremony, Alonso de Briceño was consecrated as the Bishop of Caracas, marking a significant milestone in his spiritual journey. As he donned the mitre and grasped the crosier, he became the spiritual leader of the Catholic faithful in Caracas, tasked with guiding them on the path of righteousness and fostering a deeper understanding of the Church's teachings. As Bishop, Alonso de Briceño worked tirelessly to promote the welfare of his flock, establishing schools, hospitals, and orphanages to cater to the needs of the poor and the marginalized. His selfless dedication to the service of others earned him the respect and admiration of the people, who saw in him a true embodiment of the values of the Catholic Church. The evidence of Alonso's work as a Catholic bishop is abundant and far-reaching. Historical records attest to his consecration as Bishop of Caracas, while accounts from the time period describe his unwavering commitment to the Church and its teachings. The numerous institutions he established during his tenure as Bishop stand as a testament to his dedication to the welfare of his people. In conclusion, the life and legacy of Alonso de Briceño serve as a powerful affirmation of the statement: Alonso de Briceño works as a Catholic bishop.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Bishop of Caracas", "Catholic bishop", "Roman Catholic prelate"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Bishop of Caracas", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Catholic bishop", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R2", "answer": "Roman Catholic prelate", "origin": "coverage_addition"}], "requested_slot_hint": "other"}
